topic: ~describe_games()
language: enu

proposal: %describeYes  Great! Let me tell you about our three games. \pau=1500\
    $showVideo=outbreak.mp4 Game number one: Outbreak. \pau=1000\ This is our scariest zombie game. \pau=400\ If you like adrenaline, \pau=300\ this game is for you. \pau=500\ A virus has turned people into zombies, \pau=400\ and your team must fight together to survive. \pau=3000\
    $showVideo=farcry.mp4 Game number two: Far Cry V R. \pau=2000\ This is a pirate survival game. \pau=300\ It has amazing visuals, \pau=300\ and a really chill vibe. \pau=400\ It's set on a dangerous island. \pau=500\ A gang of pirates has captured you, \pau=400\ and your team must work together to escape. \pau=3000\
    $showVideo=spacemarines.mp4 Game number three: Space Marine V R. \pau=1000\ This is a science fiction battle. \pau=500\ You are a powerful space soldier, \pau=400\ and your team must defend the planet from an alien army. \pau=1500\ This game has two modes. \pau=400\ A thirty minute mode, \pau=300\ or a harder forty five minute mode. \pau=400\ The harder mode adds challenges like friendly fire, \pau=300\ and you can revive your teammates. \pau=2000\
    Those are our games! $onStopped=1

proposal: %describeNo. Okay, no problem. $onStopped=2

u:([yes "yes please" sure "go ahead" "describe them" okay]) ^gotoReactivate(describeYes)
u:([no "no thanks" "no thank you" "I already know" skip]) ^gotoReactivate(describeNo)

u:(e:yesAnswer) ^gotoReactivate(describeYes)
u:(e:noAnswer) ^gotoReactivate(describeNo)
